  "description": "HUGXOW crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C50 H50 Cl8 Gd4 N10 O4,C5 H5 N1. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 4 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 2 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 4 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 2 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 2 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 4 O neighbors; Gd3A (Gd) has 2 O neighbors; Gd4A (Gd) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.544-4.015 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.48-117.80°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd4(O2)2Cl8(py)10]·py.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
